  {
    "title": "Found Horizons 2 - QUIETMAN • 30 YEARS DEEP IN THE ARCHIVES",
    "artist": "Quietman",
    "genre": "Archive",
    "kind": "album",
    "img": "https://f4.bcbits.com/img/a2807768344_5.jpg",
    "url": "https://quietmanmusic.bandcamp.com/album/found-horizons-2-quietman-30-years-deep-in-the-archives",
    "embed": 132812575,
    "description": "FOUND HORIZONS – VOLUME 2\r\nQUIETMAN • 30 YEARS DEEP IN THE ARCHIVES\r\n\r\nSomewhere between the first experiments of the early 90s and the music we're making today, there's a whole universe of Quietman waiting to be rediscovered.\r\n\r\nFound Horizons – Volume 2 opens the vault once again.\r\n\r\nSpanning more than three decades of Quietman recordings, this collection brings together rare remixes, forgotten releases, tracks once heard only in live sets, studio experiments, alternative versions, lost recordings and demos from albums that never quite made it into the world.\r\n\r\nDrawn from original studio masters, archive recordings and forgotten corners of the Quietman catalogue, these are pieces from different chapters of the journey. Some may be familiar to those who've followed Quietman over the years; others have remained tucked away in the archives, waiting for another moment in the sun.\r\n\r\nFrom deep melodic journeys and atmospheric explorations to unexpected collaborations, alternative directions and beautifully strange studio detours, Found Horizons2 celebrates the many paths Quietman has travelled — including those that led somewhere unexpected.\r\n\r\nNot quite a retrospective. Not quite a rarities collection. More like discovering a parallel history of Quietman, one recording at a time.\r\n\r\nThirty years of experiments, ideas, adventures and musical horizons.\r\n\r\nSome remembered. Some forgotten. Some never heard before. All part of the journey.\r\n\r\nWelcome back to the Quietman universe.",
    "release_date": "04 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT",
    "metadata_checked": true,
    "tags": []
  },
